# Rust Idioms

Prefer the standard library and the type system over cleverness.

## Ownership First

- Model ownership before adding clones
- Borrow when the callee does not need to keep the value
- Use `clone()` only when the cost is understood and documented
- Prefer `&str` in APIs; take `String` only when storing

## Errors and Options

- Return `Result<T, E>` for recoverable failures
- Use `Option<T>` for absence, never sentinel values
- Prefer `?` over nested `match`
- Define crate-local error types; implement `From` for conversion

## Types

- Newtypes for domain values
- Enums for closed state machines
- Traits for shared behavior, not for every struct
- Keep generics readable; add `where` clauses when bounds grow

## Style

- `rustfmt` is the formatter; do not hand-format
- `clippy` warnings are errors in this repo
- No `unwrap()` / `expect()` in library paths unless the invariant is proven
- `unsafe` requires a SAFETY comment and a wrapping safe API
